# Structural control flow

**Prerequisites:** [Use directives](/docs/how-to/use-directives/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Directives](/docs/reference/language/directives/).

Rocci parses a template tree. `{expr}` is a Roc expression, not a nested
template. `{if active { <Icon /> }}` is rejected because the parser would have
to treat Roc as markup.

`@if`, `@for`, and `@match` are template forms whose arms are template items.
They lower to ordinary Roc (`if`, `List.map`, `match`) after the structure is
known. `@let` binds derived values in that same template region.

Use Roc for data decisions; use directives for markup-producing branches.

**Related:** [Text and interpolation](/docs/reference/language/text/).
